# TypeScript & React Conventions

- Strict mode; no `any` unless justified with a comment explaining why. No `as` casts to silence the compiler.
- Imports at the top of the module — no inline imports.
- Exhaustive `switch` over discriminated unions/enums with a `never` check in `default`:

```typescript
switch (status) {
  case "passed": /* ... */ break;
  case "failed": /* ... */ break;
  // ...all variants...
  default: {
    const _exhaustive: never = status;
    throw new Error(`Unhandled status: ${_exhaustive}`);
  }
}
```

- Prefer discriminated unions over boolean flags for state.
- Functional components; extract hooks only for reused interactive logic.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed.
- Domain types live in `src/core/`; UI and adapters import from core, never the reverse.
